<article class="env-remark" id="">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/">Remark <span data-tag="">6.5.4.10</span>.</a>It is tempting to try to evade the problem described above by working instead with the hypercomplete $\infty $-topoi $\Shv (X)^{\wedge }$ and $\Shv (Y)^{\wedge }$. In this case, we <em>can</em> test whether or not $u: \calF \rightarrow p_{\ast } p^{\ast } \calF $ is an equivalence by passing to stalks. However, since the proper base change theorem does not hold in the hypercomplete context, the stalk $(p_{\ast } p^{\ast } \calF )_{y}$ is not generally equivalent to the global sections of $p^{\ast } \calF | X_{y}$. Thus, we still encounter difficulties if we want to deduce global consequences from information about the individual fibers $X_{y}$. </p>
